+# Native mobile Turnstile page
+
+The Vexlune Hub iOS client loads the same-origin HTTPS route
+`/mobile/turnstile`. This is a normal public frontend route containing only
+the official Cloudflare Turnstile widget and a constrained
+`ReactNativeWebView.postMessage` bridge. It is not a login page and it does not
+introduce a private captcha exchange endpoint.
+
+The page reads `GET /api/v1/settings/public` and uses only the public
+`turnstile_site_key`. The native app supplies a fresh `version`, `requestId`,
+`nonce`, and action (`login`, `register`, or `forgot_password`) in the URL
+fragment. Every bridge message repeats and is checked against that tuple. The
+token is passed once to the existing auth endpoint as `turnstile_token`; the
+official backend remains the only component that calls Cloudflare Siteverify.
+The Secret Key stays in the backend configuration and is never present in the
+frontend bundle, route fragment, or app package.
+
+## Deployment checklist
+
+1. Build the frontend from the reviewed commit with `pnpm build` in
+   `frontend/`. The build writes `backend/internal/web/dist`; deploy that
+   bundle with the existing Sub2API release process.
+2. Keep the normal SPA fallback enabled for `/mobile/turnstile`, while making
+   sure the route is not redirected to `/login` and that `/api/v1/settings/public`
+   remains JSON.
+3. Keep the existing CSP. It already allows the official script and iframe:
+   `https://challenges.cloudflare.com` in `script-src` and `frame-src`. Do not
+   add `unsafe-eval`, arbitrary origins, or a proxy for Cloudflare's script.
+4. Purge only stale HTML/configuration caches for the site after rollout. The
+   page bundle may use normal content-hash caching; the HTML shell and public
+   settings must be revalidated.
+5. Confirm the configured widget authorizes hostname `hub.vexlune.com` (hostname
+   entries contain no protocol, port, or path). Do not enable arbitrary
+   hostnames as a workaround.
+
+## Post-deployment probes
+
+Run these from a machine that can reach the production hostname:
+
+```sh
+BASE_URL="https://hub.vexlune.com"
+
+# The route must return the SPA shell with a 200 and must not redirect to login.
+curl --fail-with-body --silent --show-error --include \
+  "$BASE_URL/mobile/turnstile#version=1&requestId=v1-login-probe-abcdefgh&nonce=probe-12345678&action=login"
+
+# Public settings must remain JSON and expose no secret.
+curl --fail-with-body --silent --show-error \
+  -H 'Accept: application/json' "$BASE_URL/api/v1/settings/public"
+```
+
+The first response will contain the built app shell; route correctness is
+confirmed by loading it in a browser/WebView and observing the page's
+`ready` handshake. A shell response by itself is not token or login evidence.
+Complete one real challenge in staging or with an approved test account, then
+verify that the existing login/register endpoint accepts the token and that a
+replay is rejected. Do not put a production Secret Key or test token in logs.
+
+## Rollback
+
+If the route serves the wrong page, the SDK is blocked, or native bridge
+handshake fails, stop the mobile rollout and redeploy the previous frontend
+bundle. Restore the prior `backend/internal/web/dist` artifact and invalidate
+only the affected HTML cache. Do not disable Turnstile, bypass Cloudflare, or
+change the auth endpoints as a rollback shortcut. No database migration or
+backend version change is required by this page.
+
+Production deployment, service restart, CDN cache purge, and Cloudflare widget
+hostname/key changes require explicit operator confirmation before execution.
